{
  "schema": 1,
  "root": "ScannerFixtureLibrary",
  "_comment": [
    "INPUT (not an expectation): the fixture library ScannerConformanceTests",
    "materialises under a TempDir, and the mutations it applies between scan",
    "passes. Committed so the Rust port can build the byte-identical tree.",
    "",
    "Files are filler bytes: FolderScanner never opens a file, it only stats",
    "and classifies by extension, so `size` + `fill` + `mtime` are the whole",
    "contract. Every mtime is set explicitly and is far in the past, which",
    "makes `dateTaken` deterministic: the scanner falls back to",
    "min(creationDate, modificationDate) and creationDate is always 'now'.",
    "",
    "`initial` is applied in order; parent directories are created on demand.",
    "`dir` entries exist only for directories no file would create.",
    "",
    "Paths are compared and stored as the filesystem reports them. The",
    "Unicode/ entry is written with a \\u0301 escape on purpose: it is the",
    "DECOMPOSED (NFD) spelling of café.jpg, and the escape survives editors",
    "and git filters that would silently precompose a literal. See",
    "stable_uuid_vectors.json for why NFC and NFD derive different ids."
  ],

